# SDD-TEXT 0.1
# Authoring template for focus_agent policy contracts.
# Source: <milton-specs #N | RULES.md SECTION>  (focus_agent owns this text; Milton is a consumer)
# Ladder: L1 <this file> | L2 <named executable gate or "DEFERRED: owner, issue URL"> | L4 <runtime refusal>
# Failure-path intent: reject / stop / fail loud. Soft-landing intents that continue past a failure are forbidden.

Step J-001 "Trigger"
  intent="<the action that brings this contract into force>"
END

Step J-002 "Failure: <violated invariant>"
  intent="Reject the change or stop the process loudly; no fallback, no exemption marker, no silent continue."
END

Step J-003 "Recovery"
  intent="Fix the root cause at the source of truth, then re-run the gate; never bypass it."
END

Process PR-001 "Detection"
  owner="focus_agent"
  description="<the gate that detects the violation>"
END

Process PR-002 "Recovery Action"
  owner="focus_agent"
  description="<the loud stop or reject, and the operator-visible report>"
END

SystemAction SA-001 "<gate name>"
  owner="focus_agent"
  failure_modes="<each failure mode MUST fail loud>"
END

J-001 PRECEDES J-002
J-002 PRECEDES J-003
J-002 REALIZED_BY PR-001
J-003 REALIZED_BY PR-002
PR-001 DEPENDS_ON SA-001
